1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
We have a community outreach course this semester

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,020
Wherein our topic is the condition of dogs in campus

3
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:10,160
So we really want to know what your opinion on what is the condition of dogs in campus

4
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:12,040
And how they should be treated

5
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:16,700
I think they are quite good

6
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:22,000
The dogs here are quite taken care of

7
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:31,720
So actually we have feeding zones for them.

8
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:38,920
It's like as a campus, we don't allow the outside dog to come inside

9
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:42,520
and we have some particular dogs that are living here

10
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:46,160
and we don't push them away

11
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:52,520
So there are students, faculty members, some sharp numbers

12
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:54,660
who are even feeding them

13
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:56,600
who are taking care of them

14
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:01,020
Even if you see they have this

15
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:03,380
callers

16
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:06,520
They are taken care of

17
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:10,300
so they don't meet with accidents or anything

18
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:15,520
So it's like they are taken care of and I think it's their birth place.

19
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:20,560
So they should tend to be moved from here.

20
00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:24,320
So what do you mean, should dogs be allowed inside the camp?

21
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:28,440
Actually, this is how they were born.

22
00:01:31,460 --> 00:01:33,940
We can't forcefully move them anywhere.

23
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:38,480
They have been living here since their birth.

24
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:43,940
So if we will relocate them, it is good for them.

25
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:48,940
We can relocate the dogs that are not allowed to be in the outside world.

26
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:51,500
But relocating them is not an option.

27
00:01:52,380 --> 00:01:54,600
What do you think is important of having a dog?

28
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:59,480
Like let the living ones stay and sterilize everyone.

29
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:01,780
Why do you think dogs are important?

30
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:03,860
Can't you see how friendly she is?

31
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:08,100
I just feed him a packet of biscuits.

32
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:11,920
I was safe, so I thought she might be hungry.

33
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:14,880
So I fed her and then she followed me.

34
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,760
Is there a feeding zone nearby or did you feed her like this?

35
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:20,500
Right now, I have fed her with my hands.

36
00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:22,960
Otherwise we had feeding zones.

37
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:26,500
We also received a mail that mentioned feeding zones.

38
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:34,480
But it's not possible that she feeds herself there every time.

39
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:41,180
Are you aware of any organizations like CCF run for campus dogs and...

40
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:46,300
I don't know about campus because I haven't been there in 2 months.

41
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:52,280
And apart from that, as you can see, she is friendly but everybody is scared of dogs.

42
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:57,640
Actually, everyone is scared of dogs but this is an accident.

43
00:02:58,300 --> 00:02:59,620
If I am not scared then it's okay.

44
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:00,800
They won't scare me.

45
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:05,260
If you are scared they will scare you more because we can sense the fear.

46
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:08,600
How do you react to when people are so scared?

47
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:09,820
Because there are dog accidents.

48
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:13,980
Have you been across any such accident where a dog bites someone or something?

49
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:20,720
Actually, when we attack them, they feel that we are harming them.

50
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:22,380
Otherwise, they won't harm us.

51
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:26,480
They know that I am not harming them.

52
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:32,200
But if he thinks that he can come to kill me or do something, obviously, he will do it in self-defense.

53
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:38,100
So, its our responsibility as a human being to understand their language.

54
00:03:38,540 --> 00:03:40,820
Okay. So, we should be more considerate towards them?

55
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:41,160
Yeah.

56
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:44,940
Because we can't replace them.

57
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:49,840
They are very friendly creatures, the most friendly creature.

58
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:52,500
So they are very good.

59
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:57,460
You should keep dogs inside the camp because they are an integral part of your community.

60
00:03:57,860 --> 00:04:01,600
They are outside our hostel and they are so friendly that I can sit in front of them and pet them.

61
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:03,660
Outside the castle bar.

62
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:07,540
There is a dog outside the castle bar called Black and White.

63
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:16,720
They are very friendly. I have to drop them outside and come back after dropping them twice.

64
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,280
They want biscuits.

65
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:26,560
The majority of the people are scared of dogs and hence it becomes difficult for them to manage dogs inside the camp.

66
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:29,600
They will be managed by the hostels.

67
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:33,520
Many people do not believe that this is well managed.

68
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:39,320
When they enter a hostel or canteen, they drop the filter and dustbins

69
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,760
and create sanitation issues.

70
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:44,440
If we feed them properly in proper feeding areas

71
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:46,340
their stomachs are full

72
00:04:46,340 --> 00:04:48,800
then they won't do such things

73
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:51,800
Do you think it should be a designated shelter for dogs

74
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:55,840
that they should be allowed to roam around?

